{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>A continual burnt offering for your generations.</b> They shall do so when they come into the land of Canaan, for they offered burnt offerings only fifty days in the wilderness of Sinai. This is the continual burnt offering that was made at Mount Sinai (Numbers 28:6), for the Tabernacle was set there at the bottom of the mountain at the edge of the camp, for the tribes were intermingled, for on the first day of the second month they began to determine the count of every tribe to make them into standards. After they journeyed a three days' distance from Mount Sinai, the Ark journeyed in the midst of the camps. And by way of reasoning, Israel did not offer burnt offerings and sacrifices except at Sinai alone, and on the Day of Atonement in the second year, for thus it is written concerning the service of Aaron: \"and he did as YHWH commanded Moses\" (Leviticus 16:34). And likewise it is written: \"Did you bring Me sacrifices and meal offerings forty years in the wilderness, O house of Israel?\" (Amos 5:25). For Israel remained in the wilderness, in desolation, a howling waste, for some thirty-eight years. From where would they have had every day half a hin of olive oil, and likewise wine, and how would they carry with them some fourteen thousand hin? And from where would they have two yearling lambs every day, plus additions for Sabbath and festivals? And there is no objection from the words \"we and our cattle\" (Numbers 20:19), for that was at Kadesh, and there they purchased from a settled area, and in that year they plundered Midian and the land of Sihon and Og, and all of them had much livestock." "Now behold, this explains the reason why it is called the Tent of Meeting." "<b>For you.</b> For Israel, and likewise the calling of the assembly." "<b>To speak to you.</b> To you alone there. And Yefet said אשר אועד לכם [where I will meet with you] refers to Moses and Aaron occasionally, but לדבר אליך [to speak to you] hints at Moses always. And His meeting ונועדתי שמה לבני ישראל [I will meet there with the children of Israel]."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The reading 'thirty-eight years' is the plain sense of the hyper-literal 'like eight and thirty years'; the syntax of the clause is compressed and Ibn Ezra's logic here is famously cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:20.929914616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}